to-rafael-pass-source : List Word
to-rafael-pass-source = lines-of (cons "# Rafael Pass"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Professor at Tel Aviv University (since 2023) and Cornell Tech, also affiliated with the Technion. ACM Fellow (2023). Your research is cryptography where it meets computational complexity and game theory."
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for every piece of your work hyperactivity builds on. Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What your work established"
  (cons ""
  (cons "For forty years cryptography rested on a catalog: factoring, discrete logarithms, lattices, each primitive tied to the algebraic problem its designers happened to trust. With Yanyi Liu you replaced the catalog with one question about information. One-way functions exist if and only if time-bounded Kolmogorov complexity is mildly hard on average (FOCS 2020). The 2021 paper, which won the CRYPTO best paper award, moved toward basing cryptography on EXP ≠ BPP. *Hardness Along the Boundary* proves that, under a strengthened derandomization assumption, one-way functions exist exactly when the boundary problem is not in ioBPP, and that the probabilistic variant pK^t gives the same characterization unconditionally. The ITCS 2026 paper reaches the characterization for the standard randomized K^t under E ⊄ ioSIZE[2^{o(n)}], and gives the first worst-case to average-case reduction for exact K^poly, through Goldberg–Sipser compression."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The field reads this as one more equivalence in meta-complexity. It says a secret exists exactly when compressibility cannot be measured efficiently. Cryptography stops being a list of trusted puzzles and becomes a theorem about the structure of information."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your consensus work does the same for distributed ledgers. With Seeman and shelat (Eurocrypt 2017) you took Nakamoto's protocol and stated what it guarantees as properties, consistency, chain growth and chain quality, proven under explicit delay and adversary bounds. With Elaine Shi, the sleepy model counted honest majority among the parties actually online, and Thunderella separated a fast optimistic path from a slow path that is always safe. A protocol trusted on intuition became a protocol with declared properties and proofs."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity takes up from it"
  (cons ""
  (cons "**One assumption, named.** As Avik put it (2026-11-18): “the interaction system can model crypto primitives & hardness assumptions as well.” In the paper a requirement is a chosen dependent family and its proof a term"
  (cons (cite s1-p24 "(§1),")
  (cons "and premises it does not prove stay explicit"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "The store's own identity of content holds under a stated collision-resistance or injectivity assumption"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p3 "(§10.8).")
  (cons "With your theorem, every primitive built from one-way functions can be stated over one hypothesis about K^t at the boundary, and a codebase that holds programs with their proofs and dependency certificates"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p6 "(§10.8)")
  (cons "shows which constructions rest on it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Protocols with declared properties.** A distributed program is an ordinary term: network choices include delivery, duplication, loss and partition, and safety is a dependent type over every finite list of adversarial choices"
  (cons (cite s10-10-p3 "(§10.10).")
  (cons "Its induction principle builds the proof from the invariant and its preservation by every adversarial step, and liveness and convergence need their own assumptions about choices and fairness; they do not follow from safety"
  (cons (cite s10-10-p4 "(§10.10).")
  (cons "The paper's long-only order and ledger program states its invariant and transition rules exactly, and makes the exchange handler's contract a premise of the correspondence, not a consequence of the state invariant"
  (cons (cite s10-10-p5 "(§10.10).")
  (cons "Consistency, chain growth and chain quality are properties of that kind: types a ledger implementation inhabits, with the delay and adversary bounds as premises. Sleepy participation and Thunderella's optimistic and fallback paths are constructions whose safety is a theorem over their own transition relation."
  (cons ""
  (cons "Avik built a language for arbitrary market-data protocols with Gašper Ažman at Citadel Securities; this is where that line of work meets yours."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why this reaches you first"
  (cons ""
  (cons "Your work went down to what has to be true for anything to be secure. Hyperactivity is built the same way, from equality and computation upward. Your result is the one it needs to make cryptography a single named dependency rather than a catalog of beliefs."
  (cons ""
  (cons "You hold full credit for the characterization of one-way functions by Kolmogorov hardness, its boundary refinements, and the property-based analysis of consensus. Where hyperactivity states them, it states them as yours. Read it looking for where it carries your theorems furthest."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Tel Aviv University profile, https://en.cs.tau.ac.il/profile/rafaelp"
  (cons "- Cornell Tech profile, https://tech.cornell.edu/people/rafael-pass"
  (cons "- Liu, Pass: One-way Functions and Boundary Hardness of Randomized Time-Bounded Kolmogorov Complexity, https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/2184"
  (cons "- Liu, Pass: Hardness Along the Boundary, https://eprint.iacr.org/2025/1497"
  (cons "- Liu, Pass: On One-way Functions and Kolmogorov Complexity, https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10233398"
  (cons "- Liu, Pass: On the Possibility of Basing Cryptography on EXP ≠ BPP, https://eprint.iacr.org/2021/535"
  (cons "- Pass, Seeman, shelat: Analysis of the Blockchain Protocol in Asynchronous Networks, https://eprint.iacr.org/2016/454"
  (cons "- Pass, Shi: The Sleepy Model of Consensus, https://eprint.iacr.org/2016/918"
  (cons "- Pass, Shi: Thunderella, https://eprint.iacr.org/2017/913"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
